infiltrator-software (0.3.92) unstable; urgency=high

  * Unify editable deb822 APT-source parsing so repository inventory and
    enable/disable mutation agree on continuation fields, comments and stanza
    identity instead of maintaining subtly different parsers.
  * Preserve deb822 stanza separators when adding an Enabled field, preventing
    adjacent repository stanzas from being merged during enable/disable edits.
  * Split read-only source inventory from privileged source mutation at the
    CMake link boundary so the graphical application no longer carries source
    mutation code merely to display configured repositories.
  * Force automatic APT-maintenance simulation into the stable C locale before
    parsing its machine-readable removal plan, avoiding locale-dependent silent
    no-op maintenance on translated hosts.
  * Keep assertions active in canonical Release-mode regression executables so
    checks and side-effecting test setup cannot disappear under NDEBUG.
  * Replace expression-spelling source contracts with durable architecture,
    authorization, release and dependency-boundary checks; add regression
    coverage for continued deb822 source fields and invalid duplicate fields.
  * Cancel superseded verification runs by Git ref and contract-test the
    build-once publication path so an older same-version main commit cannot race
    the current state into a release.

 -- Shannon Smith <infiltratr@yandex.com>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:30:00 +1000

infiltrator-software (0.3.91) unstable; urgency=high

  * Consolidate Debian control parsing and common ASCII text handling so package
    state, repository metadata and policy/configuration readers cannot drift.
  * Tighten GUI ownership boundaries, centralise subprocess startup, remove dead
    view dependencies and prevent graphical code from including engine internals.
  * Make canonical font assets reusable in verified offline builds and avoid
    release-tag network access during verification-only CI runs.
  * Declare the remaining apt-get executor dependency explicitly, remove the
    duplicate hand-written systemd postinst logic and make package verification
    architecture-neutral for cross-builds.
  * Collapse the single-use installed-state CMake target and add regression
    contracts for the new parser, text utilities and ownership boundaries.

 -- Shannon Smith <infiltratr@yandex.com>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:14:00 +1100

infiltrator-software (0.3.90) unstable; urgency=high

  * Build release source archives from tracked Git objects plus the exact Common
    gitlink instead of copying the working tree, preventing generated or
    untracked files from leaking into source releases.
  * Derive Debian package architecture from the verified package rather than
    hard-coding amd64 across CI, package verification and release publication.
  * Tighten CMake dependency visibility, make source/core ownership explicit,
    apply compiler warnings centrally and collapse repetitive test declarations.

